	(generator "pcbnew")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Axial resistor, 10.16 mm lead pitch, pads pre-rotated 90 deg in the footprint's own local frame (pad 1 at 0,-5.08, pad 2 at 0,+5.08) so it can be placed at rotation 0 like every other footprint in this repo - this project deliberately never uses the placement rotation token (see mkpcb.py's header note), and this project's own placement checker regex only matches a bare two-argument (at x y). Same part as TS06_R_Axial_P10.16mm_Front, just spun 90 deg at authoring time instead of at placement time.")
